IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbr-nouns`
IMPORT `cbr-reg3`
IMPORT `cbr-reg4`

-- TESTS OF REGULATION 4 (src:59-87), and of its link to regulation 3(1). Expected
-- values are read off the Table in the text: thirteen rows; rows 1 to 4 and 9 and 10
-- revoked in whole; the others in part.

§ `Tests of regulation 4`

§§ `The Table (src:61-87)`

#ASSERT `the number of rows in the Table in regulation 4` EQUALS 13

-- Revoked in whole ("The whole instrument."): rows 1, 2, 3, 4, 9, 10.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 revokes the whole of the instrument cited as` "S.I. 1976/1267."
#ASSERT `regulation 4 revokes the whole of the instrument cited as` "S.R. 1976 No. 223."
#ASSERT `regulation 4 revokes the whole of the instrument cited as` "S.I. 1991/502."
#ASSERT `regulation 4 revokes the whole of the instrument cited as` "S.R. 1991 No. 82."
#ASSERT `regulation 4 revokes the whole of the instrument cited as` "S.I. 1998/1581."
#ASSERT `regulation 4 revokes the whole of the instrument cited as` "S.R. 1998 No. 239."
-- Revoked in part only: rows 5, 6, 7, 8, 11, 12, 13.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 revokes part only of the instrument cited as` "S.I. 1993/965."
#ASSERT `regulation 4 revokes part only of the instrument cited as` "S.R. 1993 No. 169."
#ASSERT `regulation 4 revokes part only of the instrument cited as` "S.I. 1996/1803."
#ASSERT `regulation 4 revokes part only of the instrument cited as` "S.R. 1996 No. 288."
#ASSERT `regulation 4 revokes part only of the instrument cited as` "S.I. 2000/1483."
#ASSERT `regulation 4 revokes part only of the instrument cited as` "S.R. 2001 No. 108."
#ASSERT `regulation 4 revokes part only of the instrument cited as` "S.I. 2005/2919."
-- Whole and part are exclusive.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 4 revokes the whole of the instrument cited as` "S.I. 1993/965.")
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 4 revokes part only of the instrument cited as` "S.I. 1976/1267.")
-- An instrument the Table does not list is not revoked by it, in whole or in part.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 4 revokes the whole of the instrument cited as` "S.I. 2006/965.")
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 4 revokes part only of the instrument cited as` "S.I. 2006/965.")
-- The row for the extent in words: row 7 is "Regulations 5 and 6."
#ASSERT any (GIVEN row YIELD (row's `citation` EQUALS "S.I. 1996/1803.") AND (row's `extent of revocation` EQUALS (`part of the instrument` "Regulations 5 and 6."))) `the Table in regulation 4`
#ASSERT any (GIVEN row YIELD (row's `citation` EQUALS "S.I. 2005/2919.") AND (row's `extent of revocation` EQUALS (`part of the instrument` "Articles 13 and 14."))) `the Table in regulation 4`

§§ `Regulation 3(1) (src:52-54) names two of the revoked instruments, and they are revoked in whole`

-- The title in the Table begins "The ": the text of regulation 3(1) writes "the" before it in running prose.
#ASSERT any (GIVEN row YIELD (row's `instrument` EQUALS (CONCAT "The ", "Child Benefit and Social Security (Fixing and Adjustment of Rates) Regulations 1976")) AND (row's `extent of revocation` EQUALS `the whole instrument`)) `the Table in regulation 4`
#ASSERT any (GIVEN row YIELD (row's `instrument` EQUALS (CONCAT "The ", "Child Benefit and Social Security (Fixing and Adjustment of Rates) Regulations (Northern Ireland) 1976")) AND (row's `extent of revocation` EQUALS `the whole instrument`)) `the Table in regulation 4`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN name YIELD any (GIVEN row YIELD (row's `instrument` EQUALS (CONCAT "The ", name)) AND (row's `extent of revocation` EQUALS `the whole instrument`)) `the Table in regulation 4`) `the earlier Regulations named in regulation 3(1)`
